GROWTH GAPS

1. Lead Magnet and Keyword Automation: Competitors like @nick_saraev and @dhavalkataria_ drive massive engagement by offering high-value assets such as prompt libraries, design systems, and funnels in exchange for a simple comment like PROMPT or CFO. @garvit.irl discusses building funnels and using AI prompts in spoken transcripts but fails to include explicit comment-to-DM triggers in the provided caption strategy, missing out on algorithmic boosts from comment volume.

2. Hook Specificity and Immediate Value: Top creators such as @favourite.engineer and @arshman open their videos with high-impact, specific pain points or shocking claims, such as Claude building websites to pay rent or smart home camera breaches. In contrast, @garvit.irl opens videos with conversational throat-clearing and general statements about the frustration of writing prompts, which causes early drop-offs in viewer retention.

3. Visual Demonstration over Talking Head: While @garvit.irl relies heavily on conversational direct-to-camera delivery about what he is currently building on his screen, top-performing competitors show the exact tool, interface, or code execution in real-time. Creators like @nick_saraev walk viewers step-by-step through specific platforms like Replit Design, keeping visual stimulation high throughout the entire duration of the short-form video.

RECOMMENDED ACTIONS

1. Implement Comment-to-DM Lead Magnets: For the next video demonstrating how to write an effective prompt or build a funnel, add an explicit call to action in the caption instructing viewers to comment a specific keyword to receive the exact template or prompt structure directly in their DMs.

2. Redesign Video Hooks: Restructure the first three seconds of upcoming content to lead with a bold result or a specific AI failure rather than conversational setups. Start directly with the transformation or the problem state to capture attention before transitioning into the tutorial.

3. Increase Screen Recording Density: Shift away from static talking-head footage and dedicate at least eighty percent of video runtime to direct screen recordings of the AI tools, dashboards, and funnels being discussed, matching the visual demonstration style of top creators in the niche.
